          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "vorāgō is built on vorō 'to swallow, to devour' (Lewis & Short): a hole that swallows things up. English voracious comes from vorō."
            }
          ]
        },
